 "notes": "Redondo (DESY 07-211), arXiv:0801.1527. Headline curve: 'Helioscope (CAST)' bound in Fig. 6 (e-print file A2.pdf), extracted from the vector PDF; axis calibration verified against tick marks and the 15 keV (log10 m=4.17) dashed line marking CAST's energy window. Curve = upper limit on kinetic mixing chi vs hidden-photon mass from non-observation of X-rays in CAST (flux bound Eq. 39, Phi < 1e-5 /cm^2/s/keV in 0.5-15 keV, a conservative cap on the CAST 2007 background; no formal CL stated, CAST's underlying result is 95% CL). Solar hidden-photon flux, not DM, so no rho_DM rescaling. The drawn curve starts at log10(m/eV)=-3.2; extended to the plot frame edge (-4.18) with the exact low-mass slope chi ~ m^-2 (Eq. 37 regime). Above 15 keV (log10 m > 4.17) the author continues the line assuming the same sensitivity with no upper energy threshold; included as drawn up to log10 m = 5. Other curves in Fig. 6 (T/L-Lifetime solar energy-loss bounds, 'Gas' scenario, m.f.p. line) not reported; Lifetime bounds are the paper's secondary result. Scenario: vacuum oscillation helioscope bound (transverse modes only).",
